### Feature 1: Multi-Model Consensus Engine

#### [NEW] [services/consensus.py](file:///Users/likhith./Startup_Scope_AI/backend/app/services/consensus.py)

- `merge_reports(gemini_report, groq_report) -> ConsensusReport`
- Field-by-field comparison:
  - Numeric fields (feasibility_score): average + confidence = `1.0 - abs(delta) / max_val`
  - String fields (market_viability): if semantically identical → high confidence, else flag as "divergent"
  - List fields (gaps_identified): union of both + dedup
- Returns `ConsensusReport` with per-field `confidence` scores and `agreement_map`

#### [MODIFY] [celery_tasks.py](file:///Users/likhith./Startup_Scope_AI/backend/app/worker/celery_tasks.py)

- Replace single `generate_ai_report()` call with parallel execution:
  - `generate_ai_report()` (Gemini)
  - `generate_groq_report()` (Groq)
- Use `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` within the Celery task (both are I/O-bound HTTP calls)
- Pass both results to `merge_reports()`
- Store `gemini_report`, `groq_report`, `consensus_confidence`, and `model_agreement` in the validations row

